WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:17.333 --> 00:00:20.041
You didn't have to run away.

2
00:00:20.125 --> 00:00:22.541
Hiro.

3
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:33.708
You forgot it. Please!

4
00:00:33.791 --> 00:00:36.333
I like your bamboo sword.

5
00:00:36.416 --> 00:00:38.500
I love it!

6
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:46.583
Lee Han! What were you thinking?

7
00:00:46.666 --> 00:00:48.500
- What?
-You scared me!

8
00:00:48.583 --> 00:00:49.666
Sorry.

9
00:00:50.833 --> 00:00:53.458
I practiced kendo in the morning.

10
00:00:54.541 --> 00:00:55.916
Good morning.

11
00:00:57.166 --> 00:00:59.875
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

12
00:01:03.958 --> 00:01:06.458
Do you have any plans after work today?

13
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:11.416
Wataru wanted to drink with everyone
in Miotełka before the Golden Week.

14
00:01:11.916 --> 00:01:14.875
I'll make sure
so he won't make you sing.

15
00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:18.458
In Miotełka?

16
00:01:18.541 --> 00:01:19.375
Yes.

17
00:01:24.666 --> 00:01:27.541
I'm not feeling well today.

18
00:01:27.625 --> 00:01:29.083
Sorry.

19
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:33.833
What?

20
00:01:38.458 --> 00:01:39.833
Good morning.

21
00:01:39.916 --> 00:01:42.083
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

22
00:01:54.166 --> 00:01:56.750
- New, wipe the tables.
- All right!

23
00:02:19.333 --> 00:02:21.000
ROMANTICS ANONYMOUS

24
00:02:21.083 --> 00:02:24.208
EPISODE 5
SPECIAL ORANGETTE

25
00:02:34.625 --> 00:02:35.833
I'm sorry.

26
00:02:35.916 --> 00:02:36.833
Yes?

27
00:02:36.916 --> 00:02:38.000
This chocolate…

28
00:02:38.875 --> 00:02:41.416
Is there something wrong with her?

29
00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:43.416
No, everything is fine.

30
00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:44.833
It's delicious.

31
00:02:45.375 --> 00:02:47.083
Delicious, but…

32
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.833
I don't remember the taste like that.

33
00:02:51.583 --> 00:02:53.041
I see.

34
00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.875
What do you think has changed?

35
00:02:58.958 --> 00:03:02.625
The recipe changed 30 years ago, right?

36
00:03:03.833 --> 00:03:08.208
Would it be possible to make several pieces?
according to the old recipe?

37
00:03:08.791 --> 00:03:10.000
I'm listening?

38
00:03:10.083 --> 00:03:14.500
At my age
fainting is not unusual.

39
00:03:15.541 --> 00:03:18.416
There's nothing to make a fuss about.

40
00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:21.875
Haven't you been working late lately?

41
00:03:23.541 --> 00:03:26.083
The company won't run itself.

42
00:03:27.208 --> 00:03:30.791
It should not be underestimated
orthostatic dizziness.

43
00:03:30.875 --> 00:03:32.583
You may suddenly lose consciousness,

44
00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:36.666
when blood pressure
flowing into the brain decreases.

45
00:03:38.458 --> 00:03:40.833
But it may have something to do with the heart.

46
00:03:43.291 --> 00:03:44.458
Anyway,

47
00:03:44.541 --> 00:03:47.583
I recommend performing full tests.

48
00:03:48.416 --> 00:03:51.416
President Fujiwara told me not to talk.

49
00:03:52.250 --> 00:03:53.291
How is he feeling?

50
00:03:53.375 --> 00:03:55.291
Research is still ongoing.

51
00:03:55.375 --> 00:03:57.458
Are you sure I don't have to come?

52
00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.041
Pretend you don't know.

53
00:04:00.583 --> 00:04:04.291
He probably doesn't want you to worry.

54
00:04:04.958 --> 00:04:07.291
He's so stubborn.

55
00:04:07.958 --> 00:04:12.458
He would go so far to protect
your pride, even in front of your only son?

56
00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:15.916
All right.

57
00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:18.958
It's good to know you're with him.

58
00:04:19.041 --> 00:04:20.625
Notify me of results.

59
00:04:20.708 --> 00:04:21.541
All right.

60
00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:34.291
He's still under investigation
but I think he'll be fine.

61
00:04:34.375 --> 00:04:36.958
Why isn't Sosuke here?

62
00:04:37.041 --> 00:04:41.250
Honestly,
it's good that you're at the president's side.

63
00:04:41.791 --> 00:04:43.583
If something happened, it would be too late.

64
00:04:43.666 --> 00:04:47.208
We need to start thinking about a successor.

65
00:04:47.708 --> 00:04:48.958
Don't worry.

66
00:04:49.541 --> 00:04:51.708
We have another Fujiwara here.

67
00:04:52.791 --> 00:04:56.250
Being the son of his twin brother,
you are practically his own son.

68
00:04:56.833 --> 00:04:58.041
True?

69
00:04:58.125 --> 00:05:00.083
Please don't say that.

70
00:05:00.583 --> 00:05:01.875
You guys are exaggerating.

71
00:05:04.916 --> 00:05:08.750
What does it mean that you want?
"save someone with chocolate"?

72
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:14.041
My parents were strict
when I was a child.

73
00:05:14.125 --> 00:05:19.708
They didn't let me eat chocolate,
claiming that it is harmful to teeth and health.

74
00:05:20.291 --> 00:05:23.833
But my older sister
she saved her pocket money

75
00:05:24.625 --> 00:05:27.500
and she bought it for me after school
orange chocolates.

76
00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:33.916
That secret taste we shared
just the two of us, it was so delicious.

77
00:05:35.541 --> 00:05:36.791
And now…

78
00:05:38.625 --> 00:05:40.458
is fighting the disease.

79
00:05:42.875 --> 00:05:44.583
He's in the hospital.

80
00:05:45.291 --> 00:05:49.000
I want her to try again
chocolates from our childhood.

81
00:05:49.958 --> 00:05:51.291
Unfortunately

82
00:05:52.291 --> 00:05:55.458
it's been a long time.

83
00:05:57.375 --> 00:05:59.333
If I don't buy them here,

84
00:06:00.291 --> 00:06:03.000
I can't find them anywhere, right?

85
00:06:05.666 --> 00:06:07.708
Her time is running out.

86
00:06:10.791 --> 00:06:12.416
I guess there's nothing I can do.

87
00:06:13.416 --> 00:06:17.583
Thank you very much
if only for listening to me.

88
00:06:17.666 --> 00:06:18.500
Of course.

89
00:06:19.125 --> 00:06:20.625
Sorry.

90
00:06:33.041 --> 00:06:34.041
Boss.

91
00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:37.708
Is it possible to recreate it somehow?

92
00:06:38.541 --> 00:06:43.291
these old chocolates,
What was the client talking about?

93
00:06:44.625 --> 00:06:46.125
For example…

94
00:06:46.625 --> 00:06:49.625
Do you still have this old recipe?

95
00:06:54.083 --> 00:06:57.291
Even if Chef Kenji left the recipe,

96
00:06:57.375 --> 00:07:00.208
I don't know if I could make them.

97
00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:05.666
I'm not sure
how they tasted 30 years ago.

98
00:07:06.250 --> 00:07:09.958
I can know.

99
00:07:12.958 --> 00:07:16.666
I used to love it
orange chocolates from this store.

100
00:07:17.791 --> 00:07:23.875
It's true
that the current ones taste a little different.

101
00:07:29.208 --> 00:07:32.875
Even if there is no recipe,

102
00:07:33.958 --> 00:07:38.166
are there records about chocolatiers,
who worked here then?

103
00:07:39.333 --> 00:07:41.833
Where were they?

104
00:07:43.541 --> 00:07:45.666
Somewhere here.

105
00:07:49.208 --> 00:07:50.083
Please.

106
00:07:57.291 --> 00:07:58.250
Twenty years…

107
00:07:58.916 --> 00:08:00.500
Chocolate lovers…

108
00:08:01.541 --> 00:08:02.375
Ten years?

109
00:08:02.458 --> 00:08:03.291
CHIEF CHOCOLATE

110
00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.916
- Maybe this person?
- What?

111
00:08:08.416 --> 00:08:09.916
About 30 years ago?

112
00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:10.958
RITSUKO SAEGUSA

113
00:08:14.458 --> 00:08:15.916
Mrs. Saegusa.

114
00:08:16.416 --> 00:08:17.791
Phone number for you.

115
00:08:18.708 --> 00:08:20.041
Mrs. Saegusa.

116
00:08:21.000 --> 00:08:25.500
Phone number for you
from a store called Savior.

117
00:08:25.583 --> 00:08:26.625
Give it to me.

118
00:08:28.125 --> 00:08:30.208
This is Ritsuko Saegusa.

119
00:08:31.083 --> 00:08:33.166
I'm sorry for calling so suddenly.

120
00:08:33.250 --> 00:08:37.541
I'm Sosuke Fujiwara, president of the Savior.

121
00:08:38.291 --> 00:08:42.291
I saw the news. Kenji died, right?

122
00:08:43.166 --> 00:08:46.333
Why handsome
are they always the first to leave?

123
00:08:47.125 --> 00:08:49.166
What is it about?

124
00:08:49.666 --> 00:08:50.666
Actually

125
00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:54.666
I'm calling about a recipe from 30 years ago.

126
00:08:56.083 --> 00:09:00.833
We have a client
who urgently needs that chocolate.

127
00:09:02.958 --> 00:09:05.458
How much time do you have left?

128
00:09:23.375 --> 00:09:26.500
Good evening. I'm Fujiwara.
I called you.

129
00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:29.583
I'm sorry I forced you
until arrival.

130
00:09:29.666 --> 00:09:33.000
Are you surprised
that I look older than you thought?

131
00:09:35.166 --> 00:09:39.083
So which chocolate should I make?

132
00:09:40.916 --> 00:09:42.875
Oh my.

133
00:09:42.958 --> 00:09:44.958
It's been a while.

134
00:09:47.541 --> 00:09:48.791
Sorry.

135
00:09:56.291 --> 00:09:57.166
Yum.

136
00:10:08.791 --> 00:10:11.125
You're right. Something has changed.

137
00:10:11.666 --> 00:10:12.750
I knew it.

138
00:10:14.375 --> 00:10:16.291
What's the difference?

139
00:10:31.041 --> 00:10:33.375
Wasanbon sugar from Awa.

140
00:10:34.875 --> 00:10:37.541
Back then we used it with Sanuki.

141
00:10:38.041 --> 00:10:42.125
Both are perfect
but if I had to describe them...

142
00:10:42.208 --> 00:10:44.416
Awa has a bolder sweetness,

143
00:10:44.916 --> 00:10:47.041
Sanuki is gentler.

144
00:10:47.125 --> 00:10:48.541
Exactly.

145
00:10:49.041 --> 00:10:51.791
Can we get wasanbon from Sanuki?

146
00:10:51.875 --> 00:10:55.333
Yes, but their store is already closed.

147
00:10:55.416 --> 00:10:58.541
Do you still order from Sakaide?

148
00:10:58.625 --> 00:10:59.750
Yes.

149
00:10:59.833 --> 00:11:01.625
Call their president.

150
00:11:01.708 --> 00:11:05.083
- I'm listening?
- Tell me Saegusa is calling.

151
00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:07.625
I see.

152
00:11:15.125 --> 00:11:18.041
Yes, I'm very sorry.

153
00:11:18.125 --> 00:11:18.958
Yes.

154
00:11:19.041 --> 00:11:20.875
I give you Ms. Saegusa.

155
00:11:20.958 --> 00:11:22.791
Mrs. Saegusa?

156
00:11:22.875 --> 00:11:24.250
No, no!

157
00:11:24.333 --> 00:11:26.250
No need! Hello?

158
00:11:26.333 --> 00:11:27.666
I hear you.

159
00:11:27.750 --> 00:11:30.291
Mrs. Saegusa?

160
00:11:30.375 --> 00:11:34.625
Bring it to the Savior
wasanbon sugar from Sanuka. But now.

161
00:11:35.166 --> 00:11:36.958
Or I'll reveal that secret.

162
00:11:37.041 --> 00:11:38.375
Your company will go bankrupt.

163
00:12:04.791 --> 00:12:05.916
You are.

164
00:12:06.625 --> 00:12:10.083
Have mercy, Mrs. Saegusa.
You haven't changed anything!

165
00:12:10.625 --> 00:12:12.166
Beautiful as always.

166
00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:15.916
I don't like younger men.
Leave him and go.

167
00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:17.708
What a welcome.

168
00:12:18.208 --> 00:12:19.125
Thanks!

169
00:12:19.208 --> 00:12:21.083
Thank you!

170
00:12:22.791 --> 00:12:24.375
Okay, let's get to work.

171
00:12:24.875 --> 00:12:27.166
I will teach you, so listen carefully.

172
00:12:27.833 --> 00:12:29.750
Let's get started.

173
00:12:30.625 --> 00:12:31.458
Yes, boss.

174
00:12:47.166 --> 00:12:48.208
Thanks.

175
00:13:03.875 --> 00:13:06.250
- You help too.
- What?

176
00:13:07.833 --> 00:13:09.083
I can?

177
00:13:12.541 --> 00:13:14.166
Thank you!

178
00:13:15.041 --> 00:13:16.625
But she was happy.

179
00:13:18.541 --> 00:13:19.708
Can I really?

180
00:13:19.791 --> 00:13:21.541
- Of course.
- Really?

181
00:13:21.625 --> 00:13:22.791
- Please.
- Go ahead.

182
00:13:22.875 --> 00:13:23.708
All right.

183
00:13:25.333 --> 00:13:26.333
You can do it.

184
00:13:26.416 --> 00:13:27.875
Yes, you can do it.

185
00:13:32.416 --> 00:13:33.625
Not bad, Hana.

186
00:13:34.125 --> 00:13:35.208
Really?

187
00:13:36.791 --> 00:13:38.375
It smells amazing.

188
00:13:38.458 --> 00:13:40.708
- Natural talent, right?
- She's good.

189
00:13:43.833 --> 00:13:45.041
I'm really glad.

190
00:14:00.750 --> 00:14:03.125
Don't squeeze?

191
00:14:04.375 --> 00:14:06.375
This way?

192
00:14:08.208 --> 00:14:10.958
Try to make it smooth. No horns.

193
00:14:11.041 --> 00:14:12.250
- All right.
- No horns.

194
00:14:15.666 --> 00:14:16.916
NO!

195
00:14:17.416 --> 00:14:19.583
Not so. Yes.

196
00:14:20.083 --> 00:14:21.458
- Sorry.
- All right.

197
00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:26.416
- Look carefully.
- Yes.

198
00:14:26.916 --> 00:14:27.875
Ready?

199
00:14:29.708 --> 00:14:32.500
This way. You see?

200
00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:35.083
Oh yes.

201
00:14:36.750 --> 00:14:39.041
Yes. You understand?

202
00:14:39.916 --> 00:14:40.750
Yes.

203
00:14:42.000 --> 00:14:45.250
- Don't just stand there. Be careful.
- Yes. Sorry.

204
00:14:45.333 --> 00:14:47.416
This position is crucial. You see?

205
00:14:47.500 --> 00:14:50.916
It cannot be too low or too high.

206
00:14:55.833 --> 00:14:57.041
First the boss.

207
00:14:57.125 --> 00:14:59.500
Boss? Call me Ritsuko.

208
00:15:00.041 --> 00:15:01.291
Okay, Ritsuko.

209
00:15:01.791 --> 00:15:02.625
Please.

210
00:15:04.708 --> 00:15:06.250
Should I add ganache?

211
00:15:06.333 --> 00:15:08.833
Stand there and watch.

212
00:15:09.625 --> 00:15:10.458
All right.

213
00:15:11.500 --> 00:15:13.375
Sorry.

214
00:15:36.916 --> 00:15:39.875
Does it taste different than back then?

215
00:15:43.166 --> 00:15:44.708
Sorry.

216
00:15:44.791 --> 00:15:47.333
After the hardships of making…

217
00:15:52.541 --> 00:15:56.166
Maybe it wasn't just the sugar.

218
00:15:58.083 --> 00:16:00.083
I see.

219
00:16:01.250 --> 00:16:02.125
Is she different?

220
00:16:03.875 --> 00:16:05.750
It may taste the same

221
00:16:05.833 --> 00:16:08.833
but maybe now that I've grown up
it tastes different to me.

222
00:16:09.791 --> 00:16:12.083
Sorry about that old lady
she couldn't help.

223
00:16:12.166 --> 00:16:14.250
We are very sorry.

224
00:16:23.916 --> 00:16:25.208
Could it be here?

225
00:16:25.291 --> 00:16:26.666
Yes, thank you.

226
00:16:27.625 --> 00:16:29.583
Thank you for driving me.

227
00:16:29.666 --> 00:16:30.791
You're welcome.

228
00:16:30.875 --> 00:16:34.250
Thank you for coming.

229
00:16:34.333 --> 00:16:36.125
With pleasure.

230
00:16:37.375 --> 00:16:40.583
I haven't made chocolates for a long time.

231
00:16:40.666 --> 00:16:43.291
I felt 20 years younger.

232
00:16:45.125 --> 00:16:46.541
Funny, right?

233
00:16:47.333 --> 00:16:49.333
I'm a wrinkled old woman

234
00:16:49.416 --> 00:16:52.916
but in my heart I am still there
the same person as then.

235
00:16:53.500 --> 00:16:54.625
Me too.

236
00:16:55.500 --> 00:16:58.416
Thanks to your chocolates

237
00:16:59.000 --> 00:17:01.125
I felt like a child again.

238
00:17:01.208 --> 00:17:02.500
Correct.

239
00:17:03.041 --> 00:17:06.250
I remember that your father
he visited us often.

240
00:17:07.875 --> 00:17:11.125
Even though he was in charge
a large confectionery company,

241
00:17:11.625 --> 00:17:17.000
he always bought a lot of them, claiming
that he wants his beloved son

242
00:17:17.083 --> 00:17:19.000
had handmade chocolates.

243
00:17:20.500 --> 00:17:22.750
You have grown into a decent man.

244
00:17:23.750 --> 00:17:25.000
I'm glad

245
00:17:26.125 --> 00:17:29.750
that the Savior is still in good hands.

246
00:17:41.458 --> 00:17:43.333
Real shame.

247
00:17:43.958 --> 00:17:46.083
I was hoping it would work.

248
00:17:49.416 --> 00:17:53.208
But it's good that you've grown up
for a decent man, Mr. Director.

249
00:17:55.375 --> 00:17:57.291
It wasn't about me.

250
00:18:00.625 --> 00:18:04.125
Just about my older brother.

251
00:18:07.291 --> 00:18:12.541
He was in poor health and had no appetite.

252
00:18:13.583 --> 00:18:17.958
My father always bought it for him
his favorite orange chocolates.

253
00:18:20.250 --> 00:18:23.208
He told my brother
that they were "energy balls".

254
00:18:24.583 --> 00:18:29.291
I was very jealous of this as a child.

255
00:18:31.416 --> 00:18:36.000
When I asked him for it,
he scolded me for being spoiled.

256
00:18:39.708 --> 00:18:40.958
One day

257
00:18:41.916 --> 00:18:45.791
my brother secretly
he gave me a chocolate which he kept.

258
00:18:47.500 --> 00:18:49.250
Then it was for me

259
00:18:50.083 --> 00:18:52.500
the best thing I've ever eaten.

260
00:18:55.875 --> 00:18:59.875
That's why you worked so hard?

261
00:19:00.750 --> 00:19:05.041
You understood Reiko's feelings
better than anyone else.

262
00:19:11.083 --> 00:19:12.833
In my case…

263
00:19:15.541 --> 00:19:21.250
I selfishly took it
my brother's favorite chocolate.

264
00:19:24.083 --> 00:19:26.625
I was the stupid, obnoxious little brother.

265
00:19:29.416 --> 00:19:30.916
Chocolate…

266
00:19:32.041 --> 00:19:34.166
not only makes the recipient happy.

267
00:19:34.250 --> 00:19:36.708
It also pleases the giver, right?

268
00:19:38.000 --> 00:19:43.000
Your brother was certainly delighted,

269
00:19:43.083 --> 00:19:46.208
seeing your happy face.

270
00:19:47.916 --> 00:19:49.333
That's why I think

271
00:19:50.375 --> 00:19:54.375
that you were there
a really good little brother.

272
00:19:57.208 --> 00:19:58.250
Is that what you think?

273
00:19:58.791 --> 00:19:59.625
Yes.

274
00:20:02.083 --> 00:20:04.000
Wait a minute!

275
00:20:06.541 --> 00:20:08.375
I remembered.

276
00:20:08.875 --> 00:20:10.333
Now I remember.

277
00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:13.833
Spécial Orangette chocolate
only for children.

278
00:20:14.333 --> 00:20:19.083
Thanks to your father
a special recipe was created.

279
00:20:35.291 --> 00:20:36.708
You are.

280
00:20:38.791 --> 00:20:42.375
Just like you asked. They are ready.

281
00:20:43.833 --> 00:20:46.125
I'm sorry I keep bothering you.

282
00:20:46.208 --> 00:20:49.708
My oldest son can eat chocolates
only from this store.

283
00:20:50.916 --> 00:20:53.166
Thanks to your idea

284
00:20:53.250 --> 00:20:58.583
we are thinking about selling
healthy chocolate for children.

285
00:20:59.333 --> 00:21:00.416
What do you think?

286
00:21:11.416 --> 00:21:12.375
Please.

287
00:21:12.958 --> 00:21:14.208
- Definitely?
- Yes.

288
00:21:14.291 --> 00:21:15.666
Geez!

289
00:21:16.333 --> 00:21:17.958
Thanks.

290
00:21:55.416 --> 00:21:58.958
Apparently they used soy milk
instead of fresh cream.

291
00:22:00.750 --> 00:22:05.208
Iron contained in soy milk
combined with vitamin C in oranges

292
00:22:05.291 --> 00:22:07.208
is good for the body.

293
00:22:08.166 --> 00:22:11.416
They used to do it
special chocolates for children.

294
00:22:13.041 --> 00:22:14.541
I'm sorry for asking

295
00:22:14.625 --> 00:22:18.041
but could you do them again?

296
00:22:18.125 --> 00:22:19.500
Of course.

297
00:22:20.333 --> 00:22:22.083
We'll take care of it.

298
00:22:22.166 --> 00:22:23.041
All right.

299
00:22:43.583 --> 00:22:46.000
Before the misunderstanding builds up,

300
00:22:46.791 --> 00:22:49.000
I have something to tell you.

301
00:22:52.833 --> 00:22:54.083
So…

302
00:22:56.833 --> 00:23:01.458
I didn't mean to listen on purpose, but…

303
00:23:03.458 --> 00:23:04.625
Actually…

304
00:23:07.166 --> 00:23:09.625
I was the one at kendo school.

305
00:23:14.333 --> 00:23:16.750
It's a long story.

306
00:23:18.250 --> 00:23:19.750
Anyway,

307
00:23:20.916 --> 00:23:23.625
your declaration of love
it wasn't a failure at all.

308
00:23:26.833 --> 00:23:29.958
Hiro is a good guy.

309
00:23:31.125 --> 00:23:32.375
So once again…

310
00:23:38.291 --> 00:23:39.666
Hana?

311
00:23:42.916 --> 00:23:43.750
Hana…

312
00:23:59.583 --> 00:24:01.916
I told you, okay?

313
00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:06.375
But you didn't hear it because you were asleep.

314
00:24:18.666 --> 00:24:21.875
My heart was trembling

315
00:24:21.958 --> 00:24:27.000
When I saw your smile

316
00:24:27.083 --> 00:24:31.250
I'm afraid our relationship
It can get awkward

317
00:24:31.333 --> 00:24:32.416
"CONFESSION"

318
00:24:32.500 --> 00:24:37.458
I was speechless

319
00:24:37.541 --> 00:24:44.375
So I turned around
Tears were streaming down my face

320
00:24:44.875 --> 00:24:48.208
I want to tell you what I feel

321
00:24:48.291 --> 00:24:50.625
But when you're close

322
00:24:50.708 --> 00:24:53.250
I can't say a word

323
00:24:53.333 --> 00:24:55.875
I'm starting to hate this about myself

324
00:24:55.958 --> 00:24:58.541
I have to be brave

325
00:24:58.625 --> 00:25:01.791
So as not to regret anything

326
00:25:01.875 --> 00:25:06.083
I will slowly get closer to you

327
00:25:06.166 --> 00:25:09.291
And then I will confess

328
00:25:09.375 --> 00:25:11.875
That I love you

329
00:25:11.958 --> 00:25:16.958
I can't say a word
I hate this about myself

330
00:25:17.041 --> 00:25:19.708
I have to be brave

331
00:25:19.791 --> 00:25:22.500
So as not to regret anything

332
00:25:22.583 --> 00:25:27.333
I will slowly get closer to you

333
00:25:27.416 --> 00:25:32.625
And then I will confess

334
00:25:35.291 --> 00:25:36.875
Try it.

335
00:26:04.750 --> 00:26:06.375
It's delicious.

336
00:26:09.375 --> 00:26:11.791
It tastes like before.

337
00:26:13.041 --> 00:26:14.625
No, even better.

338
00:26:26.083 --> 00:26:27.666
Thank you.

339
00:26:28.208 --> 00:26:30.625
I can't believe you bought them for me.

340
00:26:32.208 --> 00:26:35.500
You've grown up, Reika.

341
00:26:36.583 --> 00:26:39.333
I've been an adult for a long time.

342
00:26:40.541 --> 00:26:43.666
I'm not a girl anymore
waiting for chocolate.

343
00:26:44.583 --> 00:26:46.750
You eat too.

344
00:26:47.458 --> 00:26:48.333
All right.

345
00:26:58.375 --> 00:26:59.625
She's so good.

346
00:27:21.416 --> 00:27:22.625
I have…

347
00:27:24.041 --> 00:27:26.666
a strange desire to steal.

348
00:27:28.500 --> 00:27:29.541
But…

349
00:27:32.750 --> 00:27:33.833
I…

350
00:27:34.958 --> 00:27:36.625
I want to change!

351
00:27:37.916 --> 00:27:40.541
I found someone

352
00:27:42.375 --> 00:27:43.833
who I really love.

353
00:27:45.375 --> 00:27:49.166
So I want to be someone
whom I will not be ashamed of.

354
00:27:49.250 --> 00:27:50.916
If I have flaws,

355
00:27:51.000 --> 00:27:55.625
I will swallow my pride and try to fix them.

356
00:27:58.916 --> 00:28:01.250
Before my baby is born.

357
00:28:03.000 --> 00:28:05.000
I think I understand how you feel.

358
00:28:06.083 --> 00:28:07.750
Do you also have kleptomania?

359
00:28:08.333 --> 00:28:10.708
What? That's not what I'm talking about.

360
00:28:11.375 --> 00:28:12.708
I meant

361
00:28:12.791 --> 00:28:16.708
about feeling like you want to change for someone.

362
00:28:17.500 --> 00:28:21.833
I think change takes courage.

363
00:28:23.208 --> 00:28:28.125
And your courage
it will definitely bring good changes.

364
00:28:40.833 --> 00:28:43.250
To change…

365
00:28:55.458 --> 00:28:59.166
- What? From the hostess club…
- Is Yuri your favorite hostess?

366
00:28:59.250 --> 00:29:02.000
I thought I lost them.

367
00:29:03.375 --> 00:29:04.666
They were lying on the floor.

368
00:29:04.750 --> 00:29:06.916
- Thank you.
- I found them.

369
00:29:07.000 --> 00:29:07.958
Doctor.

370
00:29:08.625 --> 00:29:09.666
I'll start

371
00:29:10.500 --> 00:29:14.666
from practicing returning items,
that I found, to their owners.

372
00:29:20.250 --> 00:29:21.833
It's mine.

373
00:29:21.916 --> 00:29:24.583
I found this on the floor.

374
00:29:24.666 --> 00:29:26.250
Thanks.

375
00:29:27.583 --> 00:29:29.083
This is my glove.

376
00:29:29.583 --> 00:29:30.625
- What?
- Oh?

377
00:29:30.708 --> 00:29:31.708
When…

378
00:29:32.583 --> 00:29:33.708
She was lying on the floor.

379
00:29:33.791 --> 00:29:35.500
- There?
- Yes.

380
00:29:35.583 --> 00:29:36.666
- What?
- All right.

381
00:29:36.750 --> 00:29:37.666
Gosh!

382
00:29:38.458 --> 00:29:40.416
You won!

383
00:29:41.166 --> 00:29:42.333
Did you eat it?

384
00:29:42.416 --> 00:29:43.666
I ate it.

385
00:29:43.750 --> 00:29:45.875
Kidding. He was lying on the floor.

386
00:29:46.625 --> 00:29:48.666
You're lucky. Point!

387
00:29:48.750 --> 00:29:50.500
Yes, point.

388
00:29:53.333 --> 00:29:55.791
What? Wait, but how?

389
00:29:55.875 --> 00:29:58.375
- What? It's mine!
- Oh…

390
00:29:58.458 --> 00:29:59.375
What about me?

391
00:30:04.541 --> 00:30:06.958
- Thank you!
- I'm so happy.

392
00:30:07.041 --> 00:30:08.666
- Yes.
- I'm glad.

393
00:30:09.250 --> 00:30:10.750
Please, Mr. Tuna.

394
00:30:13.916 --> 00:30:14.958
If you want,

395
00:30:15.750 --> 00:30:17.125
you can keep it.

396
00:30:18.416 --> 00:30:21.791
As a thank you for your courage.

397
00:30:22.333 --> 00:30:23.166
What?

398
00:30:26.500 --> 00:30:28.250
Thank you very much.

399
00:30:28.333 --> 00:30:30.583
Who made you want to change?

400
00:30:31.166 --> 00:30:32.541
Miracle Touch?

401
00:30:32.625 --> 00:30:34.125
What are you talking about?

402
00:30:34.208 --> 00:30:36.375
I told you he liked someone else.

403
00:30:36.458 --> 00:30:39.750
You're nervous. This is suspicious!

404
00:30:41.125 --> 00:30:44.958
Buy me a drink
and I will listen to you as a friend.

405
00:30:45.041 --> 00:30:47.625
I'll buy you a drink so you don't have to ask.

406
00:30:49.625 --> 00:30:51.541
All right. Where will we go?

407
00:30:52.291 --> 00:30:56.416
I can trust a friend for once
and drink until you pass out?

408
00:30:56.500 --> 00:30:58.541
I bet you always drink that much.

409
00:30:58.625 --> 00:30:59.583
Choose a place.

410
00:31:00.083 --> 00:31:01.250
All right.

411
00:31:28.416 --> 00:31:30.916
He can't practice kendo without his sword.

412
00:31:31.625 --> 00:31:34.250
True? Yes.

413
00:31:34.750 --> 00:31:37.666
I'll drop him off quietly.

414
00:31:50.958 --> 00:31:53.500
We are. Come inside. I'll park.

415
00:31:53.583 --> 00:31:55.500
Bright. Thanks.

416
00:31:56.958 --> 00:31:57.875
All right.

417
00:32:09.416 --> 00:32:10.625
What?

418
00:32:11.833 --> 00:32:12.666
Wait.

419
00:32:13.750 --> 00:32:15.125
Wait.

420
00:32:31.083 --> 00:32:33.458
It's really a coincidence.

421
00:32:34.166 --> 00:32:37.041
I'm here by mistake.

422
00:32:39.916 --> 00:32:41.166
Coincidence?

423
00:32:41.250 --> 00:32:43.500
Exactly.

424
00:32:44.000 --> 00:32:46.125
It doesn't mean anything.

425
00:32:46.208 --> 00:32:47.041
Bye.

426
00:32:47.708 --> 00:32:48.791
Your coat.

427
00:32:51.041 --> 00:32:52.666
Could you take him?

428
00:32:54.791 --> 00:32:57.500
Let there be no more
"coincidences".

429
00:32:59.916 --> 00:33:01.250
I'll take it.

430
00:33:26.500 --> 00:33:28.583
Your coat is there.

431
00:33:36.000 --> 00:33:37.583
Are you angry?

432
00:33:38.458 --> 00:33:39.458
On me?

433
00:33:41.791 --> 00:33:43.750
You're acting strange today.

434
00:33:45.500 --> 00:33:46.875
What is this?

435
00:33:48.041 --> 00:33:49.250
What do you mean?

436
00:33:50.333 --> 00:33:52.000
Are you kidding me?

437
00:33:53.416 --> 00:33:55.708
It's not like that.

438
00:33:59.666 --> 00:34:00.958
Do you like me?

439
00:34:04.958 --> 00:34:06.375
Do you hate?

440
00:34:07.666 --> 00:34:09.500
It's not that I hate you.

441
00:34:09.583 --> 00:34:10.791
So you like me?

442
00:34:13.083 --> 00:34:16.125
Why would I try to sleep with someone
Who don't I like, for the second time?

443
00:34:16.208 --> 00:34:17.666
So you like me?

444
00:34:18.166 --> 00:34:19.958
Don't confuse me.

445
00:34:22.541 --> 00:34:25.708
I have my reasons too.

446
00:34:25.791 --> 00:34:26.625
Hi.

447
00:34:31.000 --> 00:34:32.333
I won't know...

448
00:34:34.375 --> 00:34:35.708
until you tell me.

449
00:34:38.458 --> 00:34:39.791
What reasons?

450
00:34:58.083 --> 00:35:01.583
I'll put it down and leave right away.

451
00:35:02.166 --> 00:35:03.833
It'll be all right.

452
00:35:16.750 --> 00:35:18.166
Please don't look.

453
00:35:19.833 --> 00:35:21.458
Mr. Fujiwara?

454
00:35:25.333 --> 00:35:27.083
Look at me.

455
00:35:27.875 --> 00:35:29.125
Just like we practiced.

456
00:35:35.208 --> 00:35:36.041
What?

457
00:35:38.375 --> 00:35:39.208
What?

458
00:35:40.208 --> 00:35:41.250
Doctor?

459
00:35:41.833 --> 00:35:42.791
Lady doc…

460
00:35:42.875 --> 00:35:44.125
Darth Vader.

461
00:35:45.000 --> 00:35:46.250
What are you doing here?

462
00:35:46.958 --> 00:35:49.625
What is the doctor doing here?

463
00:35:51.041 --> 00:35:55.041
Well... It's a long story.

464
00:35:56.333 --> 00:35:59.666
Do you know each other?

465
00:36:00.333 --> 00:36:02.208
I want to know that too.

466
00:36:03.041 --> 00:36:06.708
Don't say Darth Vader is…

467
00:36:08.125 --> 00:36:09.500
Miracle Touch?

468
00:36:18.375 --> 00:36:19.291
Oh?

469
00:36:20.166 --> 00:36:21.291
What are you doing?

470
00:36:22.250 --> 00:36:23.083
Hi.

471
00:36:23.583 --> 00:36:26.166
Correct! It's a Wonderful Touch.

472
00:36:27.958 --> 00:36:29.208
I'll introduce you.

473
00:36:30.291 --> 00:36:34.375
She has me now
really interested.

474
00:36:53.250 --> 00:36:54.083
What?

475
00:40:43.125 --> 00:40:45.958
Subtitles: Grzegorz Marczyk

